  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening indigenous leaders and organizations in Bolivia&apos;s Amazon to protect our common home</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to respond to the interconnected socio-environmental crisis in one of the areas of Bolivian Amazon most affected by climate crisis, deforestation, forest fires, droughts and illegal mining, all of which repesent grave threats to local communities, the environment and biodiversity. The project aims to strengthen indigenous organizations from the Department of Beni in the Bolivian Amazon for the protection of the common home, in partnership with the local Catholic Church social and emergency pastoral network. Working with Indigenous leaders will develop and strengthen their abilities and skills to defend their territories and the environment through capacity training to support Environmental justice, protection and regeneration. Furthermore, the project will also contribute to strengthening Emergency preparedness, response and early recovery by indigenous communities amidst natural disasters.</narrative>
  </description>
